  "vulnerability_information": "# Description \n\nA reflected Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) vulnerability exists on the `████` search \n\n# Steps \n\n1. Visit: █████████ \n2. Enter this in the search: ```test`-alert(0)-`k ```or simply visit: ████████ \n3. XSS is Executed!\n\n## Impact\n\nAn attacker can potentially:\n\n- Steal credentials or session tokens by accessing `document.cookie` or `localStorage`.\n- Log keystrokes to capture sensitive user input, including passwords or credit card data.\n- Perform actions on behalf of authenticated users (e.g., change settings, send messages).\n- Deface parts of the UI or inject misleading content (e.g., fake login prompts).\n- Exfiltrate CSRF tokens or other DOM-accessible secrets.\n- Redirect users to malicious sites or deliver browser-based exploits.\n- Propagate the payload across users (e.g., wormable XSS in chat or profile systems).\n\n## System Host(s)\n██████\n\n## Affected Product(s) and Version(s)\n\n\n## CVE Numbers\n\n\n## Steps to Reproduce\n1. Visit: ████████ \n2. Enter this in the search: ```test`-alert(0)-`k ```or simply visit: ██████ \n3. XSS is Executed!\n\n## Suggested Mitigation/Remediation Actions\n\n\n",
